# Reranker service configuration.
#
# Copy to .env in this folder to configure `docker compose up` run FROM HERE. Running the
# root stack instead reads the repo-root .env, not this one — Compose only picks up the
# .env next to the file it was invoked with. Same variable names either way.
#
# These are the COMPOSE-level names. docker-compose.yaml maps them to the unprefixed
# names the app reads (RERANKER_MODEL_ID -> MODEL_ID), so the prefix keeps them from
# colliding with the embedding service's. Running uvicorn directly, without Compose,
# means setting the unprefixed names instead — see the right-hand column.

# --- Model ---
# Any supported reranking model. The default is Apache-2.0.               (app: MODEL_ID)
# RERANKER_MODEL_ID=Qwen/Qwen3-Reranker-0.6B

# How scores are produced. This MUST match the model's architecture:
#   causal          Qwen3-Reranker — asks the model yes/no, scores P(yes)
#   cross-encoder   BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3 and similar sequence classifiers
# A mismatch does not error, it silently returns meaningless scores — which is why the
# service scores a known-relevant and known-irrelevant pair at startup and warns if the
# ordering is wrong. Watch for that line in the logs after changing this.
#                                                                       (app: MODEL_KIND)
# Note: mxbai-rerank-large-v2 is Apache-2.0 and looks like a drop-in, but it is a Qwen2
# architecture and will NOT score correctly under `causal`.
# RERANKER_MODEL_KIND=causal

# "cpu", "cuda", or empty to let transformers decide.                 (app: MODEL_DEVICE)
# RERANKER_DEVICE=cpu

# --- Throughput and limits ---
# Query/document pairs scored per forward pass.                     (app: MAX_BATCH_SIZE)
# RERANKER_BATCH_SIZE=8

# Documents accepted in a single /v1/rerank request.                 (app: MAX_DOCUMENTS)
# RERANKER_MAX_DOCUMENTS=200

# Token budget per query/document pair. Longer costs quadratically more attention.
#                                                                      (app: MAX_LENGTH)
# RERANKER_MAX_LENGTH=4096

# --- Instruction ---
# Overrides the built-in instruction used in the scoring prompt. Leave unset to keep the
# default; an empty value is treated as unset. The surrounding prompt template is NOT
# configurable — Qwen3-Reranker was fine-tuned on that exact wording, and changing it
# degrades scores rather than erroring.                          (app: DEFAULT_INSTRUCTION)
# RERANKER_INSTRUCTION=Given a web search query, retrieve relevant passages that answer the query

# --- Access control ---
# Optional shared secret. When set, callers must send `Authorization: Bearer <key>`, and
# the backend must send the same value. Shared with the embedding service on purpose:
# both are internal services behind the same trust boundary.      (app: INFERENCE_API_KEY)
# INFERENCE_API_KEY=

# --- Not configurable here ---
# HF_HOME is fixed to /models by the Dockerfile, because docker-compose.yaml mounts
# ./models there to cache the weights across restarts. Changing one without the other
# re-downloads the model on every start.
#
# The service listens on 8000 and publishes no host port: only the backend reaches it,
# over the compose network. Add a `ports:` entry to call it directly.
